why: `getSchemeClaim` asks `LegacyLedgerKeys` for `DirectCash` in its first branch and sends every other scheme to the standard API, and the fact that the prefixed interface answers for `DirectCash` only is why; run 10 wrote the header from the other fact and routed this one to the human as fitting nowhere, while one declaration in the file performs the act it explains; the tie names the branch's interface and the scheme it asks about
labelled: 2026-09-24
--- code
export async function getSchemeClaim(requirement: SchemeRequirement, formatName: string): Promise<LedgerClaim> {
  if (window.LegacyLedgerKeys && requirement.scheme === PostingScheme.DirectCash) {
    return getClaimThroughPrefixedSchemeApi(requirement.scheme, window.LegacyLedgerKeys);
  }

  if (typeof ledgerApi.requestSchemeAccess === 'function') {
    return getClaimThroughStandardApi(requirement, formatName);
  }

  return LedgerClaim.Unknown;
}
--- facts
`LegacyLedgerKeys`, the vendor's prefixed interface, answers for DirectCash only.
On the vendor's ledgers the standard scheme API answers DirectCash as unsupported.
